//! Types moved out of `iyakki_agent::settingstools_machine` (F-SPLIT-03, scripted by dist/split/move_types.py); the agent re-exports them.



pub const PROMPT_RULE: &str = "\nMACHINE SWITCHES (administrators change, everyone reads): startup_status (administrators; free) shows which services of the machine are ready, starting or failed; system_sounds_status/system_sounds_set (the cues for sign-in, sign-out, a new notification, a finished job: master switch, level in dB below the volume, each cue), battery_settings_status/battery_settings_set (percentage in the top bar, low-battery warnings, shutdown at the critical level), power_settings_status/power_settings_set (power profile, sleep after idle minutes, sleep while busy) and cloud_mode_status/cloud_mode_set (hide what needs a local screen, speakers or camera: automatic, on or off). Status tools are free; every set tool asks first. FAN CONTROL (Settings -> Power, Macs with an applesmc fan only): fan_control_status shows whether IYAKKI or the firmware runs the fans, the hottest temperature and the fan speeds (free). fan_control_set turns it on or off and sets the curve (low, mark, max in degrees C, hysteresis) and asks first. It is off by default, was tried against a fake system folder only and never on a real Mac, and the firmware's own curve takes over again on any doubt. DOWNLOAD ADDRESSES (programs the vendor publishes no build of for IYAKKI's images, such as OpenVPN): download_source_status shows the address and SHA-256 the person gave (free); download_source_set sets or clears it (asks first, administrators) and downloads nothing: the person clicks the download in Settings, and a file whose SHA-256 differs is thrown away. VPN HELPER: vpn_helper_status shows whether the privileged helper is switched on and listening; vpn_helper_set switches it on or off (asks first; the session still runs as the same user on images, so it adds no protection yet). OUTGOING FIREWALL: firewall_outgoing_plan (administrators, free) checks rules for outgoing connections, forwarding and port forwards and shows the nft rules they would become; it applies NOTHING and you must say so. firewall_outgoing_status shows what is in force (free); firewall_outgoing_set puts rules in force (asks first; the person then has 60 seconds to press Keep on Settings -> Firewall or it is taken back). radio_settings_status/radio_settings_set show and change what the radio does when a live station drops (retries 0 to 5, default 2; auto_switch: go on to the next station of the list, default on); asks first; the first play still needs the person.";
